      "content": "but it doesn't feel like a \"cry for help.\" it feels like a reality. i tried to talk to them, to fix it, but there's just this wall. i see them laughing and being normal in groups and i realize i'm just... done. like, the version of me that belonged there is gone. what's even the point of trying to be \"seen\" when the people who actually knew me decided i don't matter? it just feels so final.",
